# Line endings: LF, everywhere, on every platform.
#
# This repository is developed on Linux and Windows. Without this file a Windows
# checkout (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites every text file to CRLF, and the first
# solution open / `dotnet test` there misbehaves: fixtures compared byte for
# byte, embedded resources, shell scripts and vendored upstream sources all
# change under it. The committed blobs are LF; these rules only stop a checkout
# from changing them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched. A native library, an audio fixture or an image with newline
# translation applied to it is silently corrupt, so these are declared rather
# than left to git's heuristic.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.so    binary
*.dylib binary
*.dll   binary
*.pdb   binary
*.a     binary
*.lib   binary
*.nupkg binary
*.xz    binary
*.gz    binary
*.zip   binary
*.wav   binary
*.mp3   binary
*.flac  binary
*.ogg   binary
*.opus  binary
*.mid   binary
*.sf2   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
